# ---- GOLDEN FIXTURE (bridge tile) ----
# resetMode=loadvm -> restore the INTERNAL 'golden' snapshot: X (-nocursor) +
# MAME 0.251 `ql` at the Sinclair QL's 80-column MONITOR-mode SuperBASIC
# screen. Nothing is typed into the fixture, and the builder asserts that: the
# QL writes command-window text in green, so a clean screen has no green in it.
#
# Two screens were answered ONCE, during the bake, and a visitor never meets
# either: MAME's imperfect-dump warning (the QL's hal16l8.ic38 PLD has never
# been dumped anywhere, so the warning is permanent) and the machine's own
# `F1...monitor / F2...TV` chooser, which the real QL insists on before it will
# draw anything else. The chooser is the exhibit's poster image instead.
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Sinclair QL (1984) in MAME's `ql` driver, resting where the machine itself stops: the 80-column MONITOR-mode SuperBASIC screen it draws once F1 is answered — window #2 a white page on the left, window #1 red on the right, the black command window along the bottom with nothing typed in it. 512x256 drawn at an exact 2x3 integer scale on the kiosk's 1024x768 X root. The QL prints no READY: it simply waits. Keyboard-only exhibit; no pointer device; QL beeper -> ALSA -> AC97.

# ---- KEYBOARD PACING (the exhibit's only input surface) ----
# The `ql` screen runs at 50.08 Hz, so the playbook's two-frame floor is 40/40.
# MEASURED on a clone of this golden (2026-08-09, 40-character lines, count of
# characters that actually landed):
#     40/40   36 of 40
#     80/80   40 of 40  (x3)
#    120/120  40 of 40  (x3)
# 40/40 is not enough here even though it is two frames: the QL's keyboard is
# not read by the CPU at all but scanned by a separate 8049 IPC and shipped to
# the 68008 over a serial link, so a keypress has to survive two sampling
# stages rather than one. This tile therefore ships one frame slower than the
# VICE tiles' bisected 80/80.
#
# The launcher's `-autoframeskip` is part of this number and must not be
# removed: without it MAME ran at 41.9% of realtime on this box and 80 ms of
# wall clock was under two EMULATED frames. See docs/guests/sinclairql.md.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=120
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=120
# No SH_KEY_MAP: MAME's default mapping already puts host ASCII on the QL
# matrix for everything the exhibit's on-screen keyboard sends.
